<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Mothe-en-Bassigny</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Mothe-en-Bassigny was a fortified town on a hilltop in the Bassigny, on the south-western border of the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, in today's Haute-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marne">Marne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. A key ducal stronghold, it was besieged several times by the French during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. After its surrender in 1645 the town and its fortifications were razed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-mazarin">Cardinal Mazarin</a>'s orders, and only ruins remain.</p></div>
